1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
1.1 Product Overview
Interlink is a digital mentorship and career development platform designed to connect individuals seeking professional guidance with experienced professionals willing to share their knowledge, skills, experiences and industry insights.
The platform addresses the challenges faced by students, recent graduates, early-career professionals, career changers and aspiring entrepreneurs who often struggle to access meaningful professional mentorship.
Unlike conventional professional networking platforms that primarily facilitate connections and content sharing, Interlink focuses on building structured, purposeful and accountable mentorship relationships.
The platform enables mentees to:
Discover credible professionals.
Identify mentors based on their career aspirations.
Request structured mentorship.
Establish development goals.
Schedule mentorship sessions.
Communicate with mentors.
Access relevant learning resources.
Track progress and development milestones.
Receive feedback and professional guidance.
Mentors can:
Create professional profiles.
Establish their areas of mentorship expertise.
Define their availability and mentee capacity.
Receive and manage mentorship requests.
Accept or decline requests.
Manage active mentorship relationships.
Create and review development goals.
Schedule sessions.
Communicate with mentees.
Monitor mentee progress.
Build professional recognition.
Administrators will oversee platform operations, mentor verification, user management, complaints, content moderation, reporting and platform quality.
1.2 Product Purpose
Interlink aims to make professional mentorship:
Accessible to individuals regardless of their existing professional networks.
Credible through professional verification and transparent profiles.
Relevant through industry and career-based discovery.
Structured through agreed objectives and mentorship plans.
Accountable through milestones and scheduled sessions.
Measurable through progress reviews and outcome tracking.
1.3 Product Philosophy
Interlink will operate around six principles:
1. Accessibility
Professional mentorship should not be limited to people with existing professional connections or privileged access to industry networks.
2. Credibility
Users should have access to reliable information about mentors' professional backgrounds, experience and verification status.
3. Compatibility
Successful mentorship depends on more than professional seniority. Industry relevance, expertise, career objectives, communication preferences and availability matter.
4. Accountability
Mentorship should involve agreed expectations, consistent engagement and measurable objectives.
5. Growth
The platform should prioritise professional development and meaningful outcomes rather than superficial engagement.
6. Safety
Users must be able to participate in an environment that promotes respect, confidentiality, responsible conduct and appropriate safeguarding.
1.4 Product Definition
Interlink is a structured mentorship ecosystem that facilitates the following journey:
Discover → Connect → Establish Goals → Learn → Apply → Track Progress → Grow.
1.5 Core Product Differentiator
Interlink is not simply a directory of experienced professionals.
Its defining feature is the ability to convert a professional introduction into a structured mentorship relationship with:
Defined expectations.
Agreed objectives.
Scheduled sessions.
Documented milestones.
Ongoing communication.
Progress reviews.
Feedback.
Measurable outcomes.
1.6 MVP Strategic Recommendation
The MVP should validate three fundamental assumptions:
Individuals are willing to seek structured professional mentorship.
Experienced professionals are willing to provide guidance through a managed platform.
Structured mentorship relationships can generate meaningful engagement and measurable development.
The MVP should prioritise the complete mentorship lifecycle.
Advanced AI, payments, built-in video conferencing, corporate programmes, social feeds and extensive learning management capabilities should not delay the initial launch.

