10. TRUST, SAFETY AND PLATFORM GOVERNANCE
Trust and safety must be part of the initial architecture rather than a feature added after launch.
10.1 Mentor Verification Framework
Interlink should distinguish between account registration, profile review and verified professional credentials.
Verification Levels
Level 1: Registered Mentor
The user has registered and completed a mentor profile.
Level 2: Profile Reviewed
The platform has reviewed the submitted professional information.
Level 3: Verified Mentor
The mentor has passed the platform's defined verification checks.
Verification should not be represented as a guarantee of competence, character or future conduct.
Verification Methods
Depending on the mentor's professional background:
Professional profile review.
Employment or organisation confirmation.
Professional website or portfolio review.
Qualification verification where relevant.
Professional references where appropriate.
Other reasonable supporting evidence.
The platform should collect only the minimum information necessary for verification.
Sensitive verification documents must not be publicly accessible.
10.2 Reporting and Blocking
Users must be able to report:
Harassment.
Discrimination.
Fraud.
Impersonation.
Misrepresentation.
Inappropriate solicitation.
Unprofessional conduct.
Suspicious messages.
Unsafe behaviour.
Inappropriate profile content.
Users should be able to block another user.
Blocking must restrict relevant communication and interaction features while preserving necessary records for legitimate investigations.
10.3 Dispute Management
Administrators must be able to:
Receive complaints.
Review relevant evidence.
Communicate with participants.
Record investigation outcomes.
Issue warnings.
Suspend accounts.
Escalate serious matters.
Close resolved cases.
Reports must have documented statuses and resolution records.
10.4 Community Guidelines
All users must agree to:
Treat other participants respectfully.
Maintain professional conduct.
Respect confidentiality.
Avoid harassment and discrimination.
Avoid misrepresenting qualifications.
Avoid inappropriate financial or personal solicitation.
Respect intellectual property.
Report suspicious activities.
Maintain appropriate professional boundaries.
10.5 Mentorship Boundaries
Interlink should clearly communicate that:
Mentors are not automatically responsible for securing employment for mentees.
Mentorship is not a guarantee of career success.
Mentors should not request unnecessary sensitive personal information.
Mentees should not be pressured into paid services.
Financial arrangements must be transparent and governed by platform policy.
Mentorship should not be misrepresented as formal therapy, legal advice or financial advice.
10.6 User Protection
The platform must provide:
Reporting and blocking.
Account suspension procedures.
Privacy controls.
Secure communications.
Clear complaint escalation.
Access to relevant community policies.
Account deactivation and deletion processes.

11. USER EXPERIENCE AND USER JOURNEYS
11.1 Registration and Onboarding Principles
Onboarding should be progressive rather than unnecessarily lengthy.
Users should first provide the information required to establish their account and basic profile.
Additional information can be collected when users discover mentors or begin a mentorship relationship.
The system should:
Save onboarding progress.
Clearly indicate completion.
Explain why information is required.
Avoid asking for information that is not needed.
Allow users to skip optional fields.
Guide users towards the next meaningful action.
11.2 Mentee Registration Journey
Visit Interlink.
Select Create Account.
Enter name, email and password.
Verify email.
Select Mentee.
Complete introductory onboarding.
Provide education and professional background.
Select career interests.
Identify development priorities.
Define mentorship expectations.
Review profile.
Complete onboarding.
Enter Mentee Dashboard.
Discover mentors.
If onboarding is incomplete, the user should be able to continue later.
11.3 Mentor Registration Journey
Visit Interlink.
Create account.
Verify email.
Select Mentor.
Complete professional profile.
Provide expertise and experience.
Define mentorship categories.
Set availability.
Set maximum mentee capacity.
Submit verification information where required.
Administrator reviews profile.
Mentor receives verification outcome.
Approved profile becomes eligible for the appropriate discovery visibility.
11.4 Mentor Discovery Journey
Open Mentee Dashboard.
Select Find a Mentor.
Search or explore recommendations.
Apply filters.
Review mentor cards.
Open a mentor profile.
Review experience, expertise and verification.
Save mentor or request mentorship.
If the mentor is unavailable, the platform should suggest alternatives.
11.5 Mentorship Request Journey
Open mentor profile.
Select Request Mentorship.
Complete request details.
Explain career objectives.
Explain why the mentor was selected.
Define expected outcomes.
Submit request.
System records pending request.
Mentor receives notification.
Mentor reviews request.
Mentor accepts, rejects or requests additional information.
If accepted, a mentorship relationship and workspace are created.
If rejected, the mentee is notified and can continue discovering other mentors.
11.6 Mentorship Activation Journey
After acceptance:
Both participants receive confirmation.
Mentorship workspace becomes available.
Participants review expectations.
They agree on communication preferences.
They establish an initial development objective.
They schedule their first session.
The system records the relationship's activation.
11.7 First Session Journey
Open mentorship workspace.
Review agreed objectives.
Propose session time.
Confirm availability.
Confirm session.
Receive reminders.
Conduct session.
Record completion and attendance.
Add session summary.
Establish next actions.
Update mentorship goals.
11.8 Goal Establishment Journey
Open active mentorship workspace.
Select Goals.
Create a development objective.
Define expected outcome.
Establish milestones.
Assign deadlines.
Begin development activities.
Submit progress updates.
Mentor reviews progress.
Complete milestones.
Review overall goal outcome.
11.9 Relationship Completion Journey
The platform must support intentional relationship closure.
Mentor or mentee initiates completion.
The other participant is notified.
Both participants review objectives.
Progress is summarised.
Outstanding milestones are recorded.
Participants provide feedback.
Relationship status changes to Completed.
Workspace history remains accessible according to retention policies.
Participants may initiate a new mentorship request if they wish to continue working together.
This process is important because mentorship should have a defined outcome, not simply remain active indefinitely.
11.10 Administrator Journey
Administrator logs in.
System validates administrative permissions.
Administrator opens dashboard.
Reviews platform metrics.
Reviews pending mentor verifications.
Reviews complaints.
Manages users and platform content.
Records relevant decisions.
System logs administrative activities.

