15. BUSINESS RULES AND PLATFORM POLICIES
This section defines platform-wide rules that must be implemented consistently across the frontend, backend and database.
15.1 Account Rules
Email addresses must be unique.
Email verification is required for protected interactions.
Users must have valid account status.
Suspended accounts cannot initiate normal platform activities.
Administrative access requires explicit permission.
15.2 Mentor Rules
Mentors must complete required professional profile information before discovery.
Verification must be represented accurately.
Mentors must define whether they are accepting new mentees.
Mentors may establish maximum mentee capacity.
Mentors may pause new requests.
Mentors must not receive requests beyond their configured capacity unless the platform explicitly allows a waitlist.
15.3 Mentee Rules
Mentees must provide sufficient information to submit meaningful mentorship requests.
Mentees must not create duplicate active relationships with the same mentor.
Mentees can manage multiple mentorship relationships where appropriate.
Mentees can withdraw pending requests.
15.4 Mentorship Rules
Every active relationship must reference a valid mentor and mentee.
Every accepted request must generate no more than one relationship.
Goals must belong to a valid mentorship.
Sessions must belong to a valid mentorship.
Conversations must be restricted to authorised participants.
Completed relationships retain their historical records according to policy.
15.5 Notification Rules
Notifications must be associated with real system events.
Duplicate notifications should be prevented.
Failed email deliveries must be logged.
Optional notifications must respect user preferences.
Security and account-related notifications may be mandatory.
15.6 Review Rules
Reviews must reference eligible mentorship participants.
Only eligible participants may submit reviews.
Private feedback must not appear publicly.
Administrators must be able to moderate reported reviews.
Reviews must not be silently altered by administrators.

