Premium Mentee Services
Potential benefits:
Advanced mentor discovery.
Enhanced progress reporting.
Additional career resources.
Priority support.
Expanded career development tools.
Core free mentorship should remain available.
20.4 Phase 3 Monetisation
Corporate Programmes
Organisations pay for managed employee mentorship programmes.
Institutional Partnerships
Universities and educational institutions pay for mentorship access and programme management.
Sponsored Mentorship
Organisations sponsor mentorship opportunities for selected communities.
Premium Career Development
Paid career assessments, learning programmes and advanced tools.
20.5 Recommended Business Model
Interlink should eventually combine:
Free mentorship.
Paid professional mentorship.
Corporate subscriptions.
Institutional partnerships.
Sponsored programmes.
Premium career development.
20.6 Monetisation Guardrails
Do not make verification dependent solely on payment.
Do not prioritise paid mentors without clear disclosure.
Do not compromise mentor credibility for commercial incentives.
Clearly communicate fees.
Establish refund and cancellation policies before accepting payments.
Avoid charging mentees before the platform demonstrates meaningful value.

