23. RISKS, ASSUMPTIONS AND DEPENDENCIES
23.1 Product Risks
Risk 1: Insufficient Mentor Supply
Mentees may join without finding suitable mentors.
Mitigation:
Recruit mentors before public launch.
Establish industry-specific mentor communities.
Introduce mentor referral initiatives.
Focus initial acquisition on selected professional sectors.
Risk 2: Low Mentor Engagement
Experienced professionals may lack sufficient time.
Mitigation:
Allow mentors to control availability.
Set mentee capacity limits.
Provide structured request information.
Make pausing requests easy.
Send relevant reminders.
Risk 3: Poor Mentee Commitment
Users may register without actively participating.
Mitigation:
Progressive onboarding.
Clear mentorship expectations.
Goal-setting.
Milestone reminders.
Engagement monitoring.
Risk 4: Misrepresentation of Credentials
Users may provide false professional information.
Mitigation:
Verification procedures.
Supporting evidence.
Reporting mechanisms.
Administrative review.
Risk 5: Harassment and Misconduct
Mentorship interactions may involve inappropriate behaviour.
Mitigation:
Reporting and blocking.
Community guidelines.
Account suspension procedures.
Complaint investigation.
Privacy controls.
Risk 6: Low Retention
Users may abandon mentorship relationships.
Mitigation:
Structured objectives.
Session reminders.
Progress reviews.
Inactivity monitoring.
Intentional relationship closure.
Risk 7: Mentor–Mentee Mismatch
A professional may have experience but not be suitable for a particular mentee.
Mitigation:
Clear expertise categories.
Career objective matching.
Transparent mentor profiles.
Structured requests.
Participant feedback.
Risk 8: Low Marketplace Liquidity
There may be sufficient users overall but insufficient mentors in specific industries or areas of expertise.
Mitigation:
Track mentor supply by category.
Launch in focused communities.
Monitor search result availability.
Recruit mentors based on demonstrated demand.
Risk 9: Technical Complexity
Excessive feature development may delay launch.
Mitigation:
Maintain strict MVP scope.
Use established integrations.
Build a modular monolith.
Defer AI, payments and video infrastructure.
Risk 10: High Operational Costs
Manual verification, support and moderation may become expensive.
Mitigation:
Establish clear operational procedures.
Prioritise high-risk cases.
Automate routine notifications.
Measure administrative workload.
Expand operations based on actual usage.
